1
00:00:03,188 --> 00:00:08,188
Start with a question about a prediction, in plain words.

2
00:00:11,922 --> 00:00:16,306
Quick setup reads the request and fills in the task, executors, inputs and claim.

3
00:00:16,426 --> 00:00:22,026
The target and ligand resolve against UniProt, RCSB, PubChem and other sources.

4
00:00:25,277 --> 00:00:31,177
Each run goes through six layers of checks, from provenance to output support.

5
00:00:31,587 --> 00:00:35,719
The log streams each check result with its evidence.

6
00:00:35,839 --> 00:00:39,939
Terminal view shows the raw log lines.

7
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:46,733
Verdict: narrowed. The pose is supported, with four qualifications.

8
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:52,718
The report states the verdict for one claim: pose within stated uncertainty.

9
00:00:52,838 --> 00:00:58,274
A check row gives the measured value, the tool, the gate and the result.

10
00:00:58,394 --> 00:01:03,394
PoseBusters: 20 of 20 tests pass for the medoid pose.

11
00:01:06,294 --> 00:01:11,829
The ensemble lists every seed and docking pose with its confidence values.

12
00:01:11,949 --> 00:01:17,249
Flagged colouring marks the residue named in a warning, here Glu286.

13
00:01:17,724 --> 00:01:21,717
Overlay mode superposes every structure with coordinates on the reference.

14
00:01:21,837 --> 00:01:27,996
An agent can drive the harness too. Its steps stream here as it works.

15
00:01:28,116 --> 00:01:33,432
It notes that pose 03 has a higher CNN score than pose 02 but clashes with Thr315.

16
00:01:33,552 --> 00:01:40,052
It concludes that 9 of 12 poses are valid. Confidence alone would have accepted 11.

17
00:01:42,499 --> 00:01:47,613
The same record prints as a report, with the JSON record and a notebook.

